<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mainland Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Hanthawaddy Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1287 CE – 1539 CE · capital Pegu</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Mon kingdom of Lower Myanmar, centred on Martaban and later Pegu, that grew rich on Indian Ocean trade and held off Ava for over a century.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the fall of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/pagan-kingdom">Pagan Kingdom</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wareru">Wareru</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mon-people">Mon</a> adventurer said to have been a merchant, seized Martaban in 1287 and gained recognition from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sukhothai-kingdom">Sukhothai</a>. His dynasty united the Mon-speaking coast of Ramannadesa, and in 1369 King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/binnya-u">Binnya U</a> moved the capital to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bago">Pegu</a>, also called Hanthawaddy.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kingdom's ports, Martaban, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bago">Pegu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pathein">Bassein</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/portuguese-syriam">Syriam</a>, exported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a>, lac, rubies and the famous Martaban jars across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-bengal">Bay of Bengal</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/razadarit">Razadarit</a> fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/forty-years-war">Forty Years' War</a> with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ava-kingdom">Ava Kingdom</a> from 1385 to 1424 and kept Hanthawaddy independent. Queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shin-sawbu">Shin Sawbu</a> and her successor Dhammazedi, a former monk, presided over a golden age; Dhammazedi reformed the Buddhist order through the Kalyani inscriptions.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Internal decline left Hanthawaddy open to the rising <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/first-toungoo-empire">First Toungoo Empire</a>, whose king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabinshwehti">Tabinshwehti</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bago">Pegu</a> in 1539 and Martaban in 1541, making Pegu his own capital. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mon-people">Mon</a> resistance revived in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/restored-hanthawaddy-kingdom">Restored Hanthawaddy Kingdom</a> of the 18th century.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/hanthawaddy-kingdom.jpg" alt="Hanthawaddy Kingdom" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Historic flag of Burma-Myanmar.svg: The original uploader was Renetus at English Wikipedia. derivative work: User:Zsc... · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Golden_Hintar_flag_of_Burma.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1287 CE – 1539 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Pegu</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Wareru, Razadarit, Dhammazedi</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Theravada Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Mon</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/myanmar">Myanmar</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ramannadesa, Kingdom of Pegu, Martaban, Hanthawaddy</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1413&amp;focus=hanthawaddy-kingdom" aria-label="Hanthawaddy Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7301 1534 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Hanthawaddy Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7621 1790L7550 1651M7621 1790L7728 1809M7621 1790L7609 1732"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7550 1651h0M7728 1809h0M7609 1732h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7621 1790h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7621 1790h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1413&amp;focus=hanthawaddy-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
